{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffSqT6AhPhGjuGnAGQ54","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate and it passes the self-check (`OK`), but expect it to rank near the bottom. Its smoke-fit ELPD-LOO is about −3075, far behind the best model's −2317.6.\n\n- **Name:** `bayes_triplet_chunk_rig_detector`\n- **Hypothesis:** People judge randomness like a Bayesian detector that sees a sequence only as a bag of its overlapping three-flip chunks. It asks whether those chunks look like even draws from all eight possible chunks (a fair coin) or like a rigged process that favours some chunks. That bag-of-chunks encoding is the one distortion: a resource limit that ignores how the chunks overlap and where they sit. Strict alternation (only HTH and THT), streaks (repeated HHH) and repeating units all look rigged; sequences with varied chunks look random.\n- **Why this one:** it targets the two discrepancies in the critique that survive the false-discovery correction. People choose the perfect alternator less often than the best model predicts, and they reward a greater variety of three-flip chunks. It also predicts that a preference for switching levels off at high switch rates.\n- **Model:** the fair-vs-rigged log-odds for each sequence is computed in `compute_features`, using a uniform prior over the rigged process's chunk probabilities. Choice is a logistic function of the left-minus-right difference, with one shared sensitivity and a small per-person left/right lean.\n\n**Changes to get under the time limit:** the first version, with a per-person sensitivity and a fitted prior concentration, ran far too slowly. The 200-iteration smoke fit took 414 s, which projects past the 30-minute admission limit. Dropping only the per-person sensitivity made it slower still, and the check timed out after nearly 10 minutes. Fixing the prior at uniform and keeping one shared sensitivity brought the check down to about 1.5 minutes.\n\n**Risks at admission:**\n- **Unreliable LOO estimate:** 1.9% of trials have Pareto k above 0.5, over the 1% tolerance, so its ELPD-LOO would be flagged as untrustworthy.\n- **Convergence:** this check runs only one chain, so R-hat was not verified.\n- **Novelty:** the novelty check was not run. It may predict close to the existing `bayes_rigged_coin_with_two_flip_memory` model, which also detects repeated triplets.\n\nFiles are in `experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_2/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2075,"cache_read_input_tokens":73216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2075,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40db528f-9c1f-4dd4-8c3b-d1f5625d8ffd","uuid":"4861c496-cb2c-4be9-a0e0-7fb2165d16ed","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:16:58.339Z","request_id":"req_011CffSqSfMaixTMyNyKDQt1"}
